{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgcJeNKe6itwsN8Z451Ui","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Item 02 is done and marked `[x]`; the kill criterion was not met.\n\n**What was done.** The three deterministic lemmas are stated and proved on paper in `reports/separator_moment.md` §2, in the numbered-step style of the first-moment report: L1 (balanced separator at exact sizes, from `exists_empty_pair_of_layout` at the prefix of size `t`), L1′ (the events `E_bip` ⊆ `E_relax`, with `3K₂` at `k = 0` as the strictness example and the proof that \"some `k`-set is in `E_bip`\" is the same event as \"an exact-size empty pair exists\"), L2 (the closed pair) and L3 (the MOSP forms). The reusable structures live in `learning/separator_moment.py`, with 21 tests in `tests/test_separator_moment.py`.\n\n**The check, before anything was called a lemma.** Every graph on 1–9 vertices (288,266), 20,000 random graphs at 10–12 and 2,000 random covers at 4–10 customers, at `k = pw` by the subset DP:\n\n| graphs | closures checked | violations |\n|---|---|---|\n| 310,266 | 4,027,298 | 0 |\n\nScript, log and summary are in `reports/scratch/separator_moment/02_lemmas/`, 113 s on 4 workers at nice 19 because the load was above 24.\n\n**Two findings beyond the item's text.**\n- **The closure stops after one round.** The item expected an iteration `A ⊆ A₁ ⊆ A₂ ⊆ …`. The Galois step gives `R₁ = V ∖ N[A]`, `A₁ = V ∖ N[R₁]`, and then `R₂ = R₁`, `A₂ = A₁`. Monotonicity holds as asserted, with equality from the second step. This corrects the item's expectation and is not a counterexample.\n- **The fixpoint is a representative, not canonical.** Closing `A` first and closing `R` first disagree on 7–10% of exact-size pairs at 7–9 vertices. The union bound needs only a map, which L2 supplies. Also, the closure's image is a proper subset of all closed pairs of the forced sizes on about 1–3% of graphs, so item 03 should report both counts.\n\n**Slack visible already at nine vertices.** At `k = pw − 1` the structures still exist on 39–46% of graphs at 7–9 vertices and on 27% of the covers, with `E_relax` adding under one point over L1.\n\n**Lean.** Seventeen Lean-ready statements are tabulated in §2.6 for item 10, each with hypotheses, conclusion and the existing lemma it rests on. The one obstacle named is the component form of `E_bip`, which needs connected components of an induced subgraph as finite sets. The pair form is cheap and is what item 08 needs.\n\n**Gate.** `gate.py` passed: Lean builds with zero `sorry` and zero `axiom`, 1,677 tests passed including the 21 new ones, pathwidth_solver 123 passed, and the paper builds with no undefined references.\n\n**Housekeeping.** PROGRESS.md has the iteration 2 entry and reads 2/13 solved. The working tree holds only the item's files, the rebuilt paper PDF from the gate, and the owner's note appended to TASK.md during the session, which concerns items 05–07, 12 and 01 and is flagged in PROGRESS.md for those sessions. Nothing was committed and nothing under `solutions/` was touched."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":607,"cache_read_input_tokens":171620,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":607,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":812,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"79d5ae08-5614-4985-8469-5dab4f20e782","uuid":"a251c4a5-88a9-4fe8-8e33-d08657ec3873","timestamp":"2026-11-01T13:42:17.885Z","request_id":"req_011CgcJeMwaAzLHNm9PkkLCS"}
